          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "*Dolmuş* literally means \"filled up\" — a vehicle that leaves as soon as its seats are taken. The word was born in Istanbul and has spread to several other languages. For going on foot there's a verb of its own: *yürüyorum*."
        },
        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Unit 6 review",
          "items": [
            "Cover the Turkish and rebuild it from memory: \"What are you doing?\" · \"I'm studying Turkish.\" · \"I don't understand.\" · \"We're waiting.\" · \"What are you drinking?\"",
            "Then make these negative: *geliyorum*, *biliyorsun*, *okuyor*, *anlıyoruz*."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
